{
  "kind": "compare",
  "id": "postgres_100k",
  "name": "Basin vs Postgres 18 (100k-row SaaS+OLAP workload, no index)",
  "claim": "At typical SaaS / OLTP scale (100k rows split across users + events), Basin's columnar substrate matches or beats Postgres heap on reads (point, range, aggregate, JOIN, ILIKE, pagination, COUNT(*), DATE_TRUNC, analytics JOIN) and pays a per-INSERT tax on bulk writes. No indexes on either side — measures substrate, not btree machinery.",
